  {
    "sha": "e95fb87e09a2e455c84110b639f18b4a4c4435ad",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKGU5NWZiODdlMDlhMmU0NTVjODQxMTBiNjM5ZjE4YjRhNGM0NDM1YWQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-24T18:06:57Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-24T18:06:57Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(motion): an Outside Arc re-entry may come down on cut floor\n\nCoordinator decision C on #3899: outside_air_check also accepts the floor\nthat is already cut at that depth, as #3855 does. A re-entry after a lift\nonto a pass start in material on an Outside pass with the Arc entry now\ncomes down in air outside the stock, or by a plunge whose tool disc is\nall on the floor already cut at that depth (the lift point first, then\nrings round the start), with a link at depth through cut floor that\ncrosses no earlier cut. Only a plunge into uncut stock is refused.\n\nPins: outside_reentry_onto_cut_floor_is_accepted,\noutside_reentry_without_an_air_lead_is_refused.\n\nRefs #3884\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "91d8bbc2489f0ff952a65f15630cc1cbc0c6118b",
