  {
    "sha": "2c5bc49d9e167e01b5b4eeb93038bfca02ce0b28",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDJjNWJjNDlkOWUxNjdlMDFiNWI0ZWViOTMwMzhiZmNhMDJjZTBiMjg",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-24T18:08:29Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-24T18:08:29Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(motion): cut floor of a re-entry is the whole disc, cut earlier\n\n\"Already cut\" now means: the moves posted before the re-entry (earlier in\nthe program order), at or below its depth, sweep the whole tool disc\nround the plunge point (the centre, a ring at half a radius and the rim\neach within one tool radius of an earlier cut's centre path). A disc cut\nonly in part does not count.\n\nPins: outside_reentry_onto_a_partly_cut_disc_is_refused,\noutside_reentry_onto_floor_cut_later_is_refused.\n\nRefs #3884\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
